{"title":"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e486e74b04f4bd209f89e7fbcfddf5da13e61844.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\left( 1 + \\frac 12 + \\frac 14 + \\frac 18 + \\frac 1{16} \\right) \\left( 1 + \\frac 13 + \\frac 19\\right) \\left( 1 + \\frac 15\\right) \\left( 1 + \\frac 17\\right) \\left( 1 + \\frac 1{11} \\right) \\left( 1 + \\frac 1{13}\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"652\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5e23478e31b53adb822e6d2aad7363ec9fc66bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\left( 1 - \\frac 12\\right)^{-1} \\left( 1 - \\frac 13 \\right)^{-1} \\left(1 - \\frac 15\\right)^{-1} \\left(1 - \\frac 17\\right)^{-1} \\left(1-\\frac 1{11}\\right)^{-1} \\left(1 - \\frac 1{13}\\right)^{-1},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"609\" height=\"46\" /></center>\n<p>and\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269f02ea71e5d27d5957d40740300477d0a605db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 1 + \\frac 12 + \\frac 13 + \\frac 14 + \\frac 15 + \\frac 16 + \\frac 17 + \\frac 18 + \\frac 19 + \\frac 1{10} + \\frac 1{11} + \\frac 1{12} + \\frac 1{13} + \\frac 1{14} + \\frac 1{15} +\\frac 1{16}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"644\" height=\"37\" /></center>\n<p>Then which of the following inequalities is true?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98e41e3f9d1b5077255187c05cbfc2846c13db22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } A &gt; B &gt; C \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } B &gt; A  &gt; C \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } C &gt; B &gt; A \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } C &gt; A &gt; B \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } B &gt; C &gt; A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"752\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you imagine expanding out the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Expression\" title=\"Expression\">expression</a> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, you can see that every term in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> will appear once, along with plenty of others.  (Think of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_factorization\" title=\"Prime factorization\">prime factorizations</a> and you can figure out which products give the terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.)  Since all terms are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d5d939964c0b0c89069819f245d2f8960bc571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &gt; C$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d9500b762c626e3b7b09c26d17cfb7ea279131c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac AB = \\left( 1 - \\frac 12\\right)\\left( 1 + \\frac 12 + \\frac 14 + \\frac 18 + \\frac 1{16} \\right) \\left( 1 - \\frac 13 \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"372\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706efef5ac55619cf96515757fc6c0a2b70f3623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 1 + \\frac 13 + \\frac 19\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"102\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/7486c029743392be6cf5ebb15e09b45b66bd525f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(1 - \\frac 15\\right) \\left( 1 + \\frac 15\\right) \\left(1 - \\frac 17\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"214\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/039465299dd8ad7a7e918cfe9cbbc684f3a531b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 1 + \\frac 17\\right) \\left(1-\\frac 1{11}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"149\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/1738c28fa87f3090efaddbe50077217ec8536628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 1 + \\frac 1{11} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"76\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/8539914a33924fce52a67ea2684238d3f39813aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(1 - \\frac 1{13}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"76\" height=\"43\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/1603146802de46444fe39e5af6ece66489489965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 1 + \\frac 1{13}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"76\" height=\"43\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c2a335c1d8dd37ebf67757c2ac1c14a5cd215b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\left(1 - \\frac1{32}\\right)\\left(1 - \\frac1{27}\\right)\\left(1 - \\frac1{25}\\right) \\left(1-\\frac1{49}\\right)\\left(1-\\frac1{121}\\right)\\left(1-\\frac1{169}\\right) &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"562\" height=\"43\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4daec1b65b2c7204eba605d45b19b072005b0218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &lt; B$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Putting these two facts together, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92c937bdeb614d98a45a6085a88ccbec018eee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B &gt; A &gt; C \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(B) \\ }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_21\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 21\">Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_23\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 23\">Next Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam\">Back to Exam</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017130656\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 67/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4493/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3448:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017130656 and revision id 19252. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}